{"raw": {"https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9128": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Electrical/Computer Engineering", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Electrical/Computer Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Assistant Professor of Electrical/Computer Engineering Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must be submitted online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com and include the following materials: Cover letter describing their interest in the position and qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Teaching statement (no more than two pages) describing teaching interests, experience, and approach to undergraduate teaching and student mentorship; preparation to teach a broad range of Electrical Engineering and Computer Engineering courses, including laboratory-based courses; potential to develop new or enhanced undergraduate courses in their area of specialization; and approach to assessing and improving student learning. Research statement (no more than two pages) summarizing research accomplishments and future research plans, including plans for establishing a productive research program that meaningfully involves and mentors undergraduate students. Academic transcripts. Names and email addresses of three professional references. References will be contacted to provide letters of recommendation through the online application system. Full consideration will be given to applications completed by December 11, 2026. Applications received after that date may be considered until the position is filled. For more information, please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Christine Zakzewski at christine.zakzewski@scranton.edu. For further information about the Physics & Engineering Department, visit our web page at https://www.scranton.edu/academics/cas/physics-engineering/index.shtml Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Electrical/Computer Engineering Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Physics & Engineering Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The Department of Physics & Engineering at The University of Scranton invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position beginning in August 2027 . Responsibilities include teaching a broad range of undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses for majors, as well as general education courses, with a teaching load of 9\u201312 credits per semester; maintaining an active research program; advising and mentoring students; contributing to program assessment and development across the department\u2019s four ABET -accredited engineering programs and two physics programs; and providing service to the University. Essential Duties The ideal candidate will demonstrate: A commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student mentorship, ideally supported by prior undergraduate teaching experience. The ability to teach a broad range of courses within the undergraduate Electrical Engineering and Computer Engineering programs. The ability to develop new or enhanced undergraduate courses that build on their areas of expertise and expand the curriculum. A record of sustained research/scholarship with demonstrated capacity to mentor undergraduate students. Practical, hands-on engineering skills or relevant industry experience. A commitment to program assessment and continuous improvement. Excellent oral and written communication skills in English. An ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Additional Skills Required Minimum Education Requirements Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a closely related field by the date of appointment. We seek candidates with demonstrated expertise in power and energy, power electronics, electrical machines and energy conversion, robotics and autonomous systems, computer architecture, or engineering applications of AI, machine learning, or cybersecurity. Candidates with expertise in closely related areas will also be considered. Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Preferred Qualifications Years of Experience Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? Yes- Please supply references at this time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00625P Open Date 10/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications must be submitted online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com and include the following materials: Cover letter describing their interest in the position and qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Teaching statement (no more than two pages) describing teaching interests, experience, and approach to undergraduate teaching and student mentorship; preparation to teach a broad range of Electrical Engineering and Computer Engineering courses, including laboratory-based courses; potential to develop new or enhanced undergraduate courses in their area of specialization; and approach to assessing and improving student learning. Research statement (no more than two pages) summarizing research accomplishments and future research plans, including plans for establishing a productive research program that meaningfully involves and mentors undergraduate students. Academic transcripts. Names and email addresses of three professional references. References will be contacted to provide letters of recommendation through the online application system. Full consideration will be given to applications completed by December 11, 2026. Applications received after that date may be considered until the position is filled. For more information, please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Christine Zakzewski at christine.zakzewski@scranton.edu. For further information about the Physics & Engineering Department, visit our web page at https://www.scranton.edu/academics/cas/physics-engineering/index.shtml Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Transcripts Optional Documents \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9111": {"title": "Faculty Specialist, Nursing", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Faculty Specialist, Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Faculty Specialist, Nursing Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for 3 references. Position Details Position Information Position Title Faculty Specialist, Nursing Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Nursing Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Scranton Department of Nursing invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure track Faculty Specialist position starting in August 2027. This in-person, on site position requires regular on-campus presence. There are opportunities to teach in the undergraduate and graduate programs; teaching and service are required. The Department of Nursing is strongly committed to excellence; the Department\u2019s graduates are recognized for being ready to deliver high-quality, evidence-based, holistic, person-centered care at all levels and across many settings. Essential Duties - Teaching - Service - Other responsibilities as outlined in the faculty contract and handbook Additional Skills Required Applicants must be licensed or eligible to be licensed as a Registered Nurse in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Minimum Education Requirements A master\u2019s degree in nursing is required. Preferred Education A doctoral degree in nursing is preferred. Minimum Job Experience Requirements Applicants must have a minimum of 3 years of recent professional nursing practice experience. Preferred Qualifications Years of Experience 3 Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Faculty Specialist Tenure Non-Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00623P Open Date 09/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for 3 references. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Reference Contact Information Optional Documents Other Document \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9110": {"title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Crime, Justice, &amp; Security", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Visiting Assistant Professor, Crime, Justice, &amp; Security Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Visiting Assistant Professor, Crime, Justice, & Security Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Apply online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/ . Please submit a letter of interest, contact information for 3 references, and a current C.V. Three letters of recommendation must be submitted prior to a campus visit. Please direct inquiries to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Michael Jenkins ( michael.jenkins@scranton.edu ) Position Details Position Information Position Title Visiting Assistant Professor, Crime, Justice, & Security Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Crime, Justice, & Security Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Scranton Department of Crime, Justice, & Security invites applications for a one-year, full-time appointment at the rank of Visiting Assistant Professor beginning in August 2027. Essential Duties The successful applicant will be expected to teach courses in corrections and juvenile delinquency. Strong preference will be given to those with demonstrated teaching ability and commitment to teaching a course in race and ethnic relations. The successful applicant will have the opportunity to teach and develop courses within other areas of interest as aligned with the programmatic needs of our Criminal Justice and Sociology programs as determined by departmental faculty. The teaching load is 21 credits over the fall and spring semesters. For further information about the department, visit our web page at: https://www.scranton.edu/academics/cas/soc-cj/index.shtml Additional Skills Required Minimum Education Requirements Applicants must provide evidence of effective teaching and a sound research agenda. Applicants must possess a terminal degree (Ph.D.) in criminology, criminal justice, or sociology; ABD may apply. The J.D. is not considered a terminal degree for this position. Applicants must provide evidence of effective teaching, a sound research agenda. Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience in an academic setting is preferred. Years of Experience Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Visiting One Year Tenure Non-Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? No- Do not provide references at this time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00621P Open Date 09/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Apply online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/ . Please submit a letter of interest, contact information for 3 references, and a current C.V. Three letters of recommendation must be submitted prior to a campus visit. Please direct inquiries to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Michael Jenkins ( michael.jenkins@scranton.edu ) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Reference Contact Information Letter of Interest Optional Documents \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9109": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on December 1, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Apply online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com Applicants must submit a cover letter, research statement, representative publications, curriculum vitae, graduate transcripts, evidence of teaching quality (e.g., teaching evaluations), and a statement that indicates their commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and how this informs their pedagogy. Three letters of recommendation will be requested from finalists. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Psychology Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Scranton Department of Psychology invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in clinical psychology beginning in August 2027. Essential Duties The successful applicant will conduct research, mentor students, and teach clinically focused courses including but not limited to psychopathology and courses in their area of expertise. Specialty area is open, but with a preference for child clinical, health, or clinical neuropsychology. The Department can furnish supervision toward psychology licensure, if desired. The University of Scranton is an AAUP unionized faculty. We are in northeastern Pennsylvania, in the rolling foothills of the Pocono Mountains. Scranton is a small city with a vibrant cultural community, just a two-hour drive from New York City and Philadelphia. For further information about the Psychology Department, visit our web page at http://scranton.edu/academics/cas/psychology/ For questions about this position, contact the Department Chair, Dr. Bryan Burnham (bryan.burnham@scranton.edu; 570-941-6687). Additional Skills Required Minimum Education Requirements Applicants should have a PhD, PsyD, or ABD in clinical, school, or counseling psychology from an APA - or PCSAS -accredited program. Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Preferred Qualifications Years of Experience Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00624P Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on December 1, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Apply online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com Applicants must submit a cover letter, research statement, representative publications, curriculum vitae, graduate transcripts, evidence of teaching quality (e.g., teaching evaluations), and a statement that indicates their commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and how this informs their pedagogy. Three letters of recommendation will be requested from finalists. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Graduate Transcripts Evidence of Teaching Quality Selected Publication(s) Research Statement Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Statement Optional Documents Other Document \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9108": {"title": "Assistant Professor, History of Science and Medicine", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, History of Science and Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Assistant Professor, History of Science and Medicine Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload a cover letter, CV, and contact information for 3 references by November 5, 2026. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor, History of Science and Medicine Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department History Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The History Department at The University of Scranton invites applications for a tenure-track position in the History of Science and Medicine to begin the 2027-28 academic year. Essential Duties The History Department at The University of Scranton invites applications for a tenure-track position in the History of Science and Medicine to begin the 2027-28 academic year. The successful applicant will have the ability to teach World History survey courses and upper-level courses in their respective field, which can include Science and Society, History of Science, Global Environmental history, and/or Medical History. The ideal candidate will also be able to contribute to the Health Humanities and/or Environmental Studies concentrations. The expected pre-tenure teaching load is 18 credits per year. The successful candidate will have a well-defined research agenda, and be able to contribute to the service needs of the department and university. Additional Skills Required Minimum Education Requirements - History PhD by time of appointment Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Preferred Qualifications Years of Experience Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00622P Open Date 09/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Please upload a cover letter, CV, and contact information for 3 references by November 5, 2026. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Reference Contact Information Optional Documents \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9051": {"title": "Faculty Specialist - Counseling &amp; Human Services (12 months)", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Faculty Specialist - Counseling &amp; Human Services (12 months) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Faculty Specialist - Counseling & Human Services (12 months) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2027. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants must submit a cover letter, resume/curriculum vitae, and list of references. Position Details Position Information Position Title Faculty Specialist - Counseling & Human Services (12 months) Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Counseling and Human Services Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Scranton Department of Counseling and Human Services invites applications for an in-person, full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track Faculty Specialist position starting in August 2027. This position would support teaching across two programs within our department: Clinical Mental Health and Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling. Faculty Specialists carry a teaching load of twenty-four (24) credit hours annually. The Department of Counseling and Human Services is strongly committed to excellence; the Department\u2019s graduates are recognized for being ready to deliver high-quality, evidence-based, holistic, person-centered care at all levels and across settings. Essential Duties - Teaching - Service - Other duties as outlined in the faculty contract and handbook Additional Skills Required Applicants must be licensed, or eligible to be licensed, as a licensed professional counselor ( LPC ) in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Minimum Education Requirements A master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Counseling/Counselor Education from a Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs ( CACREP ) accredited program is required. Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Preferred Qualifications Ideal applicants will have clinical experience (5 years post master\u2019s), a professional counselor identity, higher education teaching experience, and clinical supervision experience. Candidates with expertise in a specific counseling specialty, including addictions or forensic/corrections counseling expertise, are preferred. Years of Experience 0 Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Faculty Specialist Tenure Non-Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? No- Do not provide references at this time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00619P Open Date 09/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2027. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants must submit a cover letter, resume/curriculum vitae, and list of references. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Reference Contact Information Optional Documents Other Document \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9035": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Biology - Translational Biology", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Biology - Translational Biology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Assistant Professor, Biology - Translational Biology Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested applicants must apply online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com . Review of applications will begin on October 9th. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The application must include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current curriculum vitae; (3) a teaching statement that (a) outlines your teaching experience, (b) describes your pedagogical approach to developing and administering student-centered classes, and (c) proposes undergraduate courses you can teach and/or develop at The University of Scranton; (4) a research statement that summarizes (a) your prior contributions to research, (b) your goals for developing a research program at The University of Scranton, and (c ) your approach to involving undergraduates from a variety of backgrounds with different levels of preparation in your research; (5) three selected publications, and (6) names and contact information of three individuals who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter requests will be automatically sent upon name submission. Letters of recommendation must be received prior to applicants being reviewed. We welcome applications from individuals of all beliefs, backgrounds, and identities. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Joe Brague, Chair of the Search Committee, via email at joe.brague@scranton.edu . Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor, Biology - Translational Biology Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Biology Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The Department of Biology at The University of Scranton invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Biology position beginning in August 2027. We seek candidates whose research bridges fundamental biological discovery and translational science to advance understanding of the mechanisms of normal biological function and disease. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, cellular and molecular biology, physiology, omics, and/or other preclinical biomedical disciplines. Our research programs embrace scientific investigation and understanding of all biological core concepts including evolution; structure and function; information flow, exchange, and storage; pathways and transformations of energy and matter; and systems. Essential Duties The successful candidate will contribute to the department\u2019s teaching mission by offering courses in general, cellular, and molecular biology, physiology, and/or related areas appropriate to departmental needs and the candidate\u2019s expertise. Faculty members are encouraged to develop and teach advanced courses aligned with their research expertise and scholarly interests. A successful candidate will establish an undergraduate-centered research program that investigates fundamental biological mechanisms relevant to human health, while providing meaningful research opportunities for undergraduate students. The successful candidate will also contribute service to the department, university, and broader community. Additional Skills Required Minimum Education Requirements A Ph.D. is required by the start date; postdoctoral experience is preferred. Experience and commitment to teaching undergraduates and the capability to develop an active research program that involves mentoring undergraduates is expected. The Biology Department is housed in a state-of-the-art unified science center http://www.scranton.edu/academics/sciencecenter .Visit http://www.scranton.edu/academics/cas/biology/ for more information about the Biology Department, its programs, and its faculty. Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Preferred Qualifications Years of Experience Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? Yes- Please supply references at this time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00618P Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Interested applicants must apply online at https://universityofscrantonjobs.com . Review of applications will begin on October 9th. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The application must include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current curriculum vitae; (3) a teaching statement that (a) outlines your teaching experience, (b) describes your pedagogical approach to developing and administering student-centered classes, and \u00a9 proposes undergraduate courses you can teach and/or develop at The University of Scranton; (4) a research statement that summarizes (a) your prior contributions to research, (b) your goals for developing a research program at The University of Scranton, and (c ) your approach to involving undergraduates from a variety of backgrounds with different levels of preparation in your research; (5) three selected publications, and (6) names and contact information of three individuals who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter requests will be automatically sent upon name submission. Letters of recommendation must be received prior to applicants being reviewed. We welcome applications from individuals of all beliefs, backgrounds, and identities. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Joe Brague, Chair of the Search Committee, via email at joe.brague@scranton.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Selected Publication(s) Optional Documents \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/9034": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Biology - Neuroscience", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Biology - Neuroscience Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Assistant Professor, Biology - Neuroscience Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested applicants must apply online at < https://universityofscrantonjobs.com >. Review of applications will begin on October 9th. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The application must include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current curriculum vitae; (3) a teaching statement that (a) outlines your teaching experience, (b) describes your pedagogical approach to developing and administering student-centered classes, and (c) proposes undergraduate courses you can teach and/or develop at The University of Scranton; (4) a research statement that summarizes (a) your prior contributions to research, (b) your goals for developing a research program at The University of Scranton, and (c ) your approach to involving undergraduates from a variety of backgrounds with different levels of preparation in your research; (5) three selected publications, and (6) names and contact information of three individuals who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter requests will be automatically sent upon name submission. Letters of recommendation must be received prior to applicants being reviewed. We welcome applications from individuals of all beliefs, backgrounds, and identities. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Ashley Driver, Chair of the Search Committee, via email at ashley.driver@scranton.edu . Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor, Biology - Neuroscience Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Biology Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Scranton Department of Biology invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant Professor beginning in August 2027. Essential Duties We welcome candidates broadly trained in neuroscience, with expertise in neuroanatomy preferred. Our department values student-centered teaching practices and seeks a candidate who is capable of offering courses including (but not limited to) Functional Neuroanatomy, Molecular and Cellular Neuroscience, and General Biology I & II. Additional courses may be taught within the Neuroscience Program and Biology Department. The successful candidate will also be expected to develop a sustainable undergraduate-driven research program that deepens the current offerings of our Neuroscience program and Biology Department. Our research programs embrace scientific investigation and understanding of all biological core concepts including evolution; structure and function; information flow, exchange, and storage; pathways and transformations of energy and matter; and systems. Applicants may also contribute to other programs in Biological Sciences including Biology, Biochemistry, Cell, and Molecular Biology ( BCMB ), Physiology, or Environmental Science. Additional Skills Required Minimum Education Requirements A Ph.D. is required by the start date; postdoctoral experience is preferred. The Biology Department is housed in a state-of-the-art unified science center < http://www.scranton.edu/academics/sciencecenter >. Visit < http://www.scranton.edu/academics/cas/biology/ > for more information about the Biology Department, its programs, and its faculty. Information on the Neuroscience program can be found at < https://www.scranton.edu/academics/cas/neuroscience/index.shtml >. Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Preferred Qualifications Years of Experience Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? Yes- Please supply references at this time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00617P Open Date 09/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Interested applicants must apply online at < https://universityofscrantonjobs.com >. Review of applications will begin on October 9th. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The application must include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current curriculum vitae; (3) a teaching statement that (a) outlines your teaching experience, (b) describes your pedagogical approach to developing and administering student-centered classes, and \u00a9 proposes undergraduate courses you can teach and/or develop at The University of Scranton; (4) a research statement that summarizes (a) your prior contributions to research, (b) your goals for developing a research program at The University of Scranton, and (c ) your approach to involving undergraduates from a variety of backgrounds with different levels of preparation in your research; (5) three selected publications, and (6) names and contact information of three individuals who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter requests will be automatically sent upon name submission. Letters of recommendation must be received prior to applicants being reviewed. We welcome applications from individuals of all beliefs, backgrounds, and identities. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Ashley Driver, Chair of the Search Committee, via email at ashley.driver@scranton.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Selected Publication(s) Optional Documents \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax: 570-941-4636 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://universityofscrantonjobs.com/postings/8974": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing \u2013 Tenure Track", "description": "The University of Scranton Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Marketing \u2013 Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help HR Homepage Assistant Professor of Marketing \u2013 Tenure Track Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Priority given to completed applications by 10/1/2026. Complete applications are to include a cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, unofficial transcript, job market paper, and teaching evaluation (if available). In addition, please provide a list of three references with their contact information. Job-related questions should be directed to Dr. Peter Andersen , Marketing Search Committee Chair by email at peter.andersen@scranton.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Marketing \u2013 Tenure Track Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing an educational, residential, and working environment that is free from harassment and discrimination. Members of the University community, applicants for employment or admissions, guests and visitors have the right to be free from harassment or discrimination based on race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, gender, sex, pregnancy and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, family responsibilities, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Sexual harassment, including sexual violence, is a form of sex discrimination prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. The University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational, extracurricular, athletic, or other programs or in the context of employment. The University will promptly address reports of discrimination under the University Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy ( NDAH Policy) or the Sexual Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy ( SHSM Policy) . Anyone who has questions about the above referenced policies, or wishes to report a possible violation of one of the policies should contact: Elizabeth M. Garcia Title IX Coordinator Office of Institutional Compliance & Title IX Institute of Molecular Biology & Medicine, Suite 315 elizabeth.garcia2@scranton.edu (570) 941-6645 https://www.scranton.edu/compliance-titleix/ The University of Scranton is an Equal Opportunity Employer/Educator. University Mission The University of Scranton is a Catholic and Jesuit university animated by the spiritual vision of Saint Ignatius Loyola, a tradition of excellence, and a commitment to the common good. The University is a community dedicated to the formation of students, and to the freedom of inquiry and personal development fundamental to the growth in wisdom and integrity of all who share its life. Department Management Marketing Job Purpose Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Immigration sponsorship will not be offered for this position. Two full-time faculty positions each with a 3-3 teaching load (18 credit hours per academic year). In addition to principles of marketing, the successful candidate must be capable of teaching other marketing courses, such as marketing strategy, marketing communications, marketing research, or consumer behavior. This is a 9-month position with a preferred start date of August 2027. Essential Duties Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, advising students, contributing to curriculum development and program assessment, conducting high quality scholarly research, and performing service to the Department, University, and Community. Additional Skills Required Familiarity with new advancements in marketing, quantitative research methods, data analytics, and AI application in marketing Minimum Education Requirements An earned Ph.D. in marketing from an AACSB -accredited business school with at least 18 credit hours of coursework. ABD candidates near completion will be considered. Preferred Education Minimum Job Experience Requirements Teaching assistant during Ph.D. program Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching or work experience in the field of marketing. Demonstrating oral proficiency in English language is a requirement, as mandated by state law. Years of Experience Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Annual Schedule 9 Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Tenure Track Is this posting collecting references? No- Do not provide references at this time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F00615P Open Date 08/13/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Priority given to completed applications by 10/1/2026. Complete applications are to include a cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, unofficial transcript, job market paper, and teaching evaluation (if available). In addition, please provide a list of three references with their contact information. Job-related questions should be directed to Dr. Peter Andersen , Marketing Search Committee Chair by email at peter.andersen@scranton.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Reference Contact Information Statement of Research Interests Job Market Paper Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations \u00a9 2013 The University of Scranton Scranton, Pennsylvania 18510 (570) 941-7400 Office of Human Resources | St. Thomas Hall, Suite 100 | The University of Scranton | Scranton, PA 18510-4633 | Phone: 570-941-7767 | Fax